{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":61.52000045776367,"text":"The square remembers a sea battle of 1805 near Cape Trafalgar in Spain where Admiral Nelson led the British fleet to victory but was wounded and died the same day. The city built him a column 52 meters tall so that he stands higher than everything around him. The four bronze lions at its foot arrived in 1867 and were made by Edwin Lancier, a painter famous for his animals who had never made a sculpture before. In the four corners there are pedestals and three of them carry old statues. The fourth stood empty for more than 150 years because the money for the statue it was waiting for ran out. Today it holds a new piece of modern art every couple of years and every time the city argues about whether it likes it. In the southeast corner look for the smallest police box with room for a single officer and every December since 1947 Norway has sent a huge Christmas tree here as a thank you for help during the war.","words":[{"word":"The","start":0,"end":0.3400000035762787},{"word":"square","start":0.3400000035762787,"end":0.6800000071525574},{"word":"remembers","start":0.6800000071525574,"end":1.2200000286102295},{"word":"a","start":1.2200000286102295,"end":1.6200000047683716},{"word":"sea","start":1.6200000047683716,"end":1.8799999952316284},{"word":"battle","start":1.8799999952316284,"end":2.0399999618530273},{"word":"of","start":2.0399999618530273,"end":2.359999895095825},{"word":"1805","start":2.359999895095825,"end":3.359999895095825},{"word":"near","start":3.359999895095825,"end":3.640000104904175},{"word":"Cape","start":3.640000104904175,"end":3.9000000953674316},{"word":"Trafalgar","start":3.9000000953674316,"end":4.360000133514404},{"word":"in","start":4.360000133514404,"end":4.679999828338623},{"word":"Spain","start":4.679999828338623,"end":4.920000076293945},{"word":"where","start":4.920000076293945,"end":5.579999923706055},{"word":"Admiral","start":5.579999923706055,"end":6.019999980